{
  "id": "interval-list-intersections",
  "questionId": "interval-list-intersections",
  "slug": "interval-list-intersections",
  "title": "Interval List Intersections",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Merge intervals",
  "patterns": [
    "merge intervals",
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "both lists are sorted by start time - do you need to compare every pair, or just the ones near each other in both lists?",
    "keep a pointer i into a and a pointer j into b. the intersection of a[i] and b[j], if it exists, is [max(starts), min(ends)]",
    "an intersection exists exactly when max(a[i].start, b[j].start) <= min(a[i].end, b[j].end)",
    "after checking a[i] and b[j], advance whichever interval ends first, since it can't possibly intersect anything further in the other list"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "advancing both pointers at once instead of only advancing the one whose interval ends first",
    "missing zero-length intersections where two intervals only touch at a single point, like [5,10] and [10,12] intersecting at [10,10]",
    "using min(starts) and max(ends) instead of max(starts) and min(ends) for the intersection bounds"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two lists of intervals, `a` and `b`. Each list is sorted by\nstart time and contains intervals that don't overlap within that same\nlist.\n\n**Return the list of intervals representing the pairwise intersection\nof `a` and `b`, sorted by start time.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= a.length, b.length <= 1000",
      "0 <= start <= end <= 10^9 for each interval",
      "each list is sorted by start time and contains no internal overlaps"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "one or both lists are empty",
      "intervals that only touch at a single point, producing a zero-length intersection like [5,5]",
      "an interval in a fully contains an interval in b",
      "no intervals intersect at all"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "a = [[0,2],[5,10],[13,23],[24,25]], b = [[1,5],[8,12],[15,24],[25,26]]",
        "output": "[[1,2],[5,5],[8,10],[15,23],[24,24],[25,25]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1,2],[5,5],[8,10],[15,23],[24,24],[25,25]]",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "a = [[1,3],[5,9]], b = []",
        "output": "[]",
        "expectedOutput": "[]",
        "explanation": "an empty second list means there can be no intersections"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
